","Bob initially had 3 orange and 4 white fish. He bought 17 additional fish (let \( w \) be white and \( o \) be orange, so \( w + o = 17 \)). After adding, orange fish (\( 3 + o \)) were twice the white fish (\( 2 \times (4 + w) \)):
