Yes, because ""non-red"" refers to yellow balloons. So ""twenty were not non-red"" translates to twenty were red. That makes sense. So the number of red balloons is 20. Wait, but wait, the problem says ""twenty of the balloons were not non-red."" So does that mean exactly 20 balloons are red? Because ""not non-red"" is red. So red balloons = 20. Then the rest would be yellow. But let's check again to make sure I'm not misunderstanding.

